Apache-2.0. DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code.

data/base-7616-word.json.gz and data/invoice-7616.json are the unmodified
data/word.json.gz and evidence/invoice-w2.json of research/p104-w2-stationary-followup
at SYLforge's #7616, vendored as data only; data/affected-pairs-7616.json is the
442-pair affected census pinned in that package's adapters/native.json, copied as
data. #7616 is prepared for SYLforge with substantial AI assistance (candidate
work with Claude Opus 5.5, checks with OpenAI assistance) and builds on Ali Romman's
#7605 (with OpenAI Codex), our #7611 stay drops (DreamingOfClouds with Claude),
Clear1nsight's #7612 contact rechart, Hao Yan/FanPUYen's #7604, SYLforge's #7603,
ToikY's #7546/#7544, Rohan Arun's signed #7113 caller and all contributors named in
those packages. Our #7615 (on #7613, on Clear1nsight's #7612) and #7612/#7613 supply
the courier lineage.

The courier (funded-return) move pattern is the crowd's: Clear1nsight's
#7244/#7274/#7314/#7334/#7481 funded-return chain and determinant-one
co-encoding, rohanarun's #7480 bypass and #7277, CubeJerry's #7577 ceiling
analysis, and petalas's #7326. This package only applies that pattern to two
(transit, courier) pairs on #7616.

check.py adapts the replay checks of our #7615 package. Its column-test section
is written from the description of the affected-pair tests in #7616's README and
adapter (512 forward and 512 adjoint Gaussian columns, signed Pauli action,
absolute phase, wrong-phase rejection); the Gaussian-dyadic Clifford conventions
(gate set P/D/C/X/phase, canonical frame circuit, child recipe) follow the
repository's frozen interpreter and compiler documented in main. It imports no
other package and none of the other PRs' code was run.
